	"description": "Beyond the Wandering Earth — a real-time cinematic journey from Earth's planetary engines to the Milky Way.\n\nLANDING: the Earth and its burning planetary engines; the camera glides between three designed views as you move the mouse (or pin one in the panel), and drifts slowly when you rest.\nINSPECT: orbit the engines, the space elevator, the ring station, the flagship, the Moon, Saturn or the Sun — drag to orbit, wheel to zoom.\nCINEMATIC: the full three-minute film — it plays only when you press Play in the on-screen panel. One-shot or seamless loop.\nFLIGHT: a guided flight past the engines, the elevator, the ring and the fleet — the cursor sets speed and direction.\n\nOn-screen control panel at the top edge — collapsed to a small icon until you click it, closes on click-outside or after a few seconds, desktop clock and telemetry, engines that react to your music, four quality tiers switched live, a frame-rate cap and an idle power saver. Rendering stops while the wallpaper is hidden or paused.\n\nFan work inspired by The Wandering Earth. NASA textures and models are public domain; planet maps CC BY 4.0 Solar System Scope; fonts SIL OFL.",
